  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rural Aids Prevention &amp; Dev Organization</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">My Tax my Voice Project is an initiative that will mobilize the local and indigenous community members who are the taxpayers through citizen grassroots forums to empower them with information about the devolved funds so that they can hold elected leaders, government officers and other duty holders accountable. This is aimed at ensuring proper utilization of the public devolved funds at the county level. The main objective of this project is to advance the interest of the youth and adults in the County government policies,legislations, budgets and prioritization of community projects processes and also to improve space for citizen participation. The County government act gives powers of self-governance to the people and enhance their participation in theexercise of the powers of the State and in making decisions affecting them&#x201d; (Article 174c, Constitution of Kenya). However, citizen participation is quite minimal in the county government structures living the key decisions to be made by the elected leaders and other government officers. Most of the time politicians manipulate the routine &#x201c;public participation&#x201d; ending up only inviting their political cronies to the public participation forums; the forums are again given very short notices and far much spread to an extend that member of the communitydo not attend them. The act also compels the County governments to involve the public in development of County Integrated Development Plan (CIDP) and Annual Development Plan (ADP) which contains all the countyplans for 5 years and 1 year respectively. Despite allthe above-mentioned policies and guidelines, the citizen who are the taxpayers are not offered sufficient opportunities to participate in prioritization and identification of the projects and servicesto the citizen, this could be due to lack of information about the roles of the community members as the right holders. Migori County as a devolved unit has received more than Kshs 72billion fromthe inception of the devolved government in the year 2013todate from the national treasury. The physical infrastructure, equipment,staffing and supply of essential drugs in health facilities are still in a deplorable state, our roads not passible, ECD schools not in good shape and nonproper support for agricultural sector. This may be attributed to the fact that the citizens are not involvedin the identification, monitoring and audit of the projects and services offered to the tax payers by the County government of Migori. It is therefore the reason this project is geared to empower the citizen to have information about the devolved government unitsby enhancing citizen participation at the grassroots level.</narrative>
  </description>
